Instruction: Read the segment of a merger agreement and answer the multiple-choice question by choosing the option that best characterizes the agreement.\nQuestion: When are representations and warranties required to be made according to the bring down provision?\nOption A: At Closing Only\nOption B: At Signing & At Closing\n\nMerger Agreement: Section 8.3 Conditions to Obligations of Parent and Subsidiary to Effect the Merger. The obligations of Parent and Subsidiary to effect the Merger are subject to the satisfaction or waiver by Parent at or prior to the Effective Time of the following conditions: (a) each of the representations and warranties of the Company contained in this Agreement, without considering any materiality or \u201cCompany Material Adverse Effect\u201d qualifications, shall be true and correct as of the Closing Date, except for inaccuracies that would not have a Company Material Adverse Effect; provided, however, that the representations and warranties that are specifically made as of a particular date shall be true and correct as of such date only. (b) Notwithstanding the foregoing, the representations and warranties set forth in Section 4.5 (Authority) and Section 4.6 (Capitalization) shall be true and correct in all respects as of the date hereof and as of the Closing Date. (Page 82)\nAnswer:
